iti21:5.1 starts: as if he were carried off
iti21:5.2 starts: and placed there.
iti21:5.3 starts: It’s because of clear-mindedness
iti21:5.4 starts: that beings go
iti24:6.1 starts: having wandered on
iti24:6.2 starts: then,
iti24:6.3 starts: with the ending of all fetters,
iti24:6.4 starts: he makes an end
iti25:3.1 starts: For the person who lies,
iti25:3.2 starts: who transgresses in this one thing,
iti25:3.3 starts: transcending concern for the world beyond:
iti25:3.4 starts: there’s no evil
iti29:4.1 starts: –knowing moderation in food,
iti29:4.2 starts: restraining his senses–
iti29:4.3 starts: he experiences ease:
iti29:4.4 starts: ease in body, ease
iti32:3.1 starts: Evil habits &
iti32:3.2 starts: evil views:
iti32:3.3 starts: a person, undiscerning,
iti32:3.4 starts: endowed with these two things,
iti32:3.5 starts: at the break-up of the body
iti32:3.6 starts: reappears in hell.
iti35:3.1 starts: For the sake of restraint,
iti35:3.2 starts: he, the Blessed One, taught
iti35:3.3 starts: a holy life not handed down,
iti35:3.4 starts: coming ashore
iti36:3.1 starts: For the sake of direct knowledge & full
iti36:3.2 starts: he, the Blessed One, taught
iti36:3.3 starts: a holy life not handed down,
iti36:3.4 starts: coming ashore
iti37:3.1 starts: Feeling urgency right here
iti37:3.2 starts: the wise,
iti37:3.3 starts: masterful,
iti37:3.4 starts: should investigate
iti38:6.1 starts: To the Tathāgata,
iti38:6.2 starts: two thoughts occur:
iti38:6.3 starts: safety
iti38:6.4 starts: seclusion
